netfox: give FishVFS an entry point for rebuilding its session

fishConn knows how to replace a dead session; nothing could ask it to.
FishVFS.Reconnect is that request, and it repoints this view at the session it
just built rather than leaving the panel that reconnected talking to the one
that died. CanReconnect tells a site that may be rebuilt from one handed a pair
of streams, so a caller does not offer a choice that cannot be taken.

Reconnect is deliberately not called from inside a request: a request that
reconnected on its own would turn one failure into a delay of unknown length in
the middle of a copy, with no way for the user to refuse. The choice belongs to
whoever meets ErrBroken and can ask, which is the next item in STEP14.md.

Only the view that reconnects is repointed. Another panel sharing the
connection keeps its pointer until it reconnects too, and is then handed the
session that already exists rather than a second one — covered by a test that
clones a view and reconnects both.